WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.034
-Our next guest is a very funny,

00:00:02.034 --> 00:00:03.736
Emmy-nominated actor you know

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.139
from "Saturday Night Live"
and "According to Jim."

00:00:06.139 --> 00:00:08.908
The second season of his show
"Growing Belushi"

00:00:08.908 --> 00:00:10.677
airs Wednesday nights
on Discovery.

00:00:10.677 --> 00:00:12.078
Let's take a look.

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:15.682
-Neem is a vegetable oil pressed
from the seeds of the neem tree.

00:00:15.682 --> 00:00:18.651
It repels up to 600
different types of insects.

00:00:18.651 --> 00:00:20.053 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:20.053 --> 00:00:22.888
It has been used in India
for centuries.

00:00:22.888 --> 00:00:25.591
It's safe, 100% organic,

00:00:25.591 --> 00:00:27.327
and it works just great.

00:00:27.327 --> 00:00:29.228
Okay.

00:00:29.228 --> 00:00:31.865
Here, you go, ladies.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:32.999
[ Laughter ]

00:00:32.999 --> 00:00:34.267
-Please welcome back to the show

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.335
our friend Jim Belushi.

00:00:35.335 --> 00:00:37.403
[ Cheering and applause ]
How are you, Jim?

00:00:37.403 --> 00:00:39.104
-I'm good, so good.

00:00:39.104 --> 00:00:41.006
Nice to see you, Seth.

00:00:41.006 --> 00:00:43.008
-You know, I would love,
obviously,

00:00:43.008 --> 00:00:45.111
to have you here in person,
but we are making progress.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.113
Last time we talked,
there was no audience,

00:00:47.113 --> 00:00:49.081
so at least we have that going
for us this time.

00:00:49.081 --> 00:00:50.649
[ Cheering ]
-Well, that's nice. That's nice.

00:00:50.649 --> 00:00:52.518
Last time we talked
was last year

00:00:52.518 --> 00:00:55.755
and you were the first interview
I did for "Growing Belushi"

00:00:55.755 --> 00:00:57.390
and thank you for that.

00:00:57.390 --> 00:00:59.759
It was a hit
and this second season,

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:02.095
we started last week
and it's doing great!

00:01:02.095 --> 00:01:04.464
-Now, we talked
about that last year,

00:01:04.464 --> 00:01:08.100
that you you were sort of
an accidental weed farmer.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.403
[ Laughter ]
This is not something
you had planned for yourself.

00:01:10.403 --> 00:01:13.206
Are you getting
the hang of it now?

00:01:13.206 --> 00:01:14.674
-You never get the hang of this.

00:01:14.674 --> 00:01:16.875
I mean, it is really farming,
Seth.

00:01:16.875 --> 00:01:20.980
I mean, this second season
of "Growing Belushi"

00:01:20.980 --> 00:01:25.385
is basically about us
redoing the whole farm,

00:01:25.385 --> 00:01:30.389
creating new greenhouses,
revamping the soil.

00:01:30.389 --> 00:01:34.260
We use the Fohse lights,
LED lights that we use.

00:01:34.260 --> 00:01:37.230
So the second season is really
starting all over again.

00:01:37.230 --> 00:01:41.634
I mean, it's tuition
in this business, you know?

00:01:41.634 --> 00:01:42.835
That's what my cousin says.

00:01:42.835 --> 00:01:44.537
I said, "Well, when am I going
to graduate?"

00:01:44.537 --> 00:01:47.039
[ Laughter ]

00:01:47.039 --> 00:01:48.741
-Is this true, Jim?

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.043
I read this -- you still have
never gotten high yourself.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:52.978
Is this true?

00:01:52.978 --> 00:01:54.213
-Oh, no, I microdose.

00:01:54.213 --> 00:01:55.482
[ Laughter ]
I do.

00:01:55.482 --> 00:01:57.650
I do a little bit
of a Bhang chocolate,

00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.652
like 2.5 milligrams,
to sleep at night.

00:02:00.652 --> 00:02:02.989
I do a little of my Cherry Pie
at the end of the day.

00:02:02.989 --> 00:02:06.825
I just do a little bit
to bring the anxiety down

00:02:06.825 --> 00:02:09.562
and also to help me sleep,
but I'm not like a stoner.

00:02:09.562 --> 00:02:11.831
[ Laughter ]
-But Cherry Pie is one
of your strands we talked about.

00:02:11.831 --> 00:02:14.467
Black Diamond.
Are these still popular,

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.236
your strains?
-They're very popular.

00:02:17.236 --> 00:02:20.105
The Cherry Pie is popular
for couples

00:02:20.105 --> 00:02:21.507
because it really
chills you out.

00:02:21.507 --> 00:02:23.376
I call it
the marriage counselor.

00:02:23.376 --> 00:02:24.710
[ Laughter ]
Black Diamond,

00:02:24.710 --> 00:02:28.114
my veterans love
for their spasms that they have,

00:02:28.114 --> 00:02:30.583
pain, sleep, PTSD.

00:02:30.583 --> 00:02:32.818
And then, last season,
we went down to Columbia

00:02:32.818 --> 00:02:35.187
and got these seeds
for Danny Aykroyd,

00:02:35.187 --> 00:02:36.789
so I have these
Colombian strains

00:02:36.789 --> 00:02:41.060
that we are 90 days
from harvesting.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:42.094
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.094 --> 00:02:43.496
-That sounds like a Mad Libs,

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:45.564
[ Laughter ]
that you went down to Colombia

00:02:45.564 --> 00:02:47.833
to get seeds for Dan Aykroyd.

00:02:47.833 --> 00:02:51.203
-Well, he wanted
a legendary seed

00:02:51.203 --> 00:02:53.205
to put the Blues Brothers on.
He goes,

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.975
[ As Aykroyd ]
Jimmy, it's a legendary brand,

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:56.675
the Blues Brothers.

00:02:56.675 --> 00:02:58.711
We need a legendary seed.

00:02:58.711 --> 00:02:59.378
[ Laughter ]

00:02:59.378 --> 00:03:01.247
I went, "Alright."

00:03:01.247 --> 00:03:03.482
-You have some great cameos
this year.

00:03:03.482 --> 00:03:04.651
Dan Aykroyd, as you mentioned.

00:03:04.651 --> 00:03:06.518
-Danny.
-Guy Fieri.

00:03:06.518 --> 00:03:07.620
-Oh.
-Was it fun to hang out?

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.721
I mean, obviously,
you know Danny well.

00:03:08.721 --> 00:03:10.356
Do you know Guy Fieri well?

00:03:10.356 --> 00:03:13.026
-Oh, I've known Guy
for 10 years, easy.

00:03:13.026 --> 00:03:16.262
He's just a gentleman and funny.

00:03:16.262 --> 00:03:17.797
And he was actually
doing a show.

00:03:17.797 --> 00:03:21.000
He was traveling from Seattle
to Santa Rosa

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.537
with like three buses of people
and four trucks

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.438
with cameras and kitchens
and he goes --

00:03:26.438 --> 00:03:27.806
[ As Fieri ]
Hey, Belush!

00:03:27.806 --> 00:03:29.508
[ Laughter ]
I'm coming down the 5.

00:03:29.508 --> 00:03:30.943
I see your farm's right there.

00:03:30.943 --> 00:03:31.810
Can I stop by?

00:03:31.810 --> 00:03:33.012
I went, "Sure."

00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:34.914
He showed up,
honest to God, Seth,

00:03:34.914 --> 00:03:36.883
with 18 cameras and 30 people.

00:03:36.883 --> 00:03:37.683
[ Laughter ]

00:03:37.683 --> 00:03:40.386
And so we shot us.

00:03:40.386 --> 00:03:44.156
I made some Blues Brothers-
infused ice cream for him

00:03:44.156 --> 00:03:46.960
[ Laughter ]
and then, he set up my backyard

00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:48.027
and set up a whole kitchen.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.698
We made barbecue ribs, clams.

00:03:51.698 --> 00:03:53.832
I mean, he was fun to have.

00:03:53.832 --> 00:03:55.534
So, anyway, yeah,
he's done the show.

00:03:55.534 --> 00:03:57.069
[ Laughter ]
-I will tell you something.

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:01.340
I can't imagine anything better,
if you were stoned

00:04:01.340 --> 00:04:04.009
and having a case
of the munchies,

00:04:04.009 --> 00:04:05.678
than Guy Fieri pulling up.

00:04:05.678 --> 00:04:07.247
[ Laughter ]

00:04:07.247 --> 00:04:09.348
It's like three buses
and Guy Fieri.

00:04:09.348 --> 00:04:11.551
You'd be like, "Whoa!"

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:13.719
[ Laughter ]

00:04:13.719 --> 00:04:17.123
-Well, let's just say
we ate ourselves to sleep.

00:04:17.123 --> 00:04:18.924
[ Laughter ]
I mean, we really did eat.

00:04:18.924 --> 00:04:21.227
And this ice cream I made,
he really loved.

00:04:21.227 --> 00:04:24.163
I showed them how to make
an infused ice cream.

00:04:24.163 --> 00:04:26.099
We made Orange Whip, you know,

00:04:26.099 --> 00:04:27.132
right out
of "The Blues brothers."

00:04:27.132 --> 00:04:28.400
Remember John Candy,
"Orange Whip,

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:29.535
Orange Whip, Orange Whip"?

00:04:29.535 --> 00:04:31.270
So, actually, it's right by you.

00:04:31.270 --> 00:04:33.773
It's in Massachusetts
this month, it comes out.

00:04:33.773 --> 00:04:35.407
-That's very exciting.
Now,

00:04:35.407 --> 00:04:36.742
what are some things
you've learned

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.577
in your second year
of doing this?

00:04:38.577 --> 00:04:40.413
What are some tips
you would tell people

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:41.914
who are trying to embark
on a career

00:04:41.914 --> 00:04:44.383
of being a marijuana farmer?

00:04:44.383 --> 00:04:45.150
-Don't do it.

00:04:45.150 --> 00:04:46.685
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.522
-Don't do it.
You know what?

00:04:49.522 --> 00:04:52.191
They make it seem like
a gold rush, but it is not.

00:04:52.191 --> 00:04:53.125
[ Laughter ]

00:04:53.125 --> 00:04:55.594
This is farming, Seth.
-Yeah.

00:04:55.594 --> 00:04:56.529
-I am a farmer.

00:04:56.529 --> 00:04:58.097
I am in the soil.

00:04:58.097 --> 00:05:01.400
I am creating, you know,
64° temperature soil,

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:04.003
in order for the micronutrients
to get to the roots correctly.

00:05:04.003 --> 00:05:06.572
I need to have
1,100 lumens of light,

00:05:06.572 --> 00:05:10.143
so, when the cloud goes over,
drops to 750

00:05:10.143 --> 00:05:13.713
and these Fohse lights
go up to compensate,

00:05:13.713 --> 00:05:15.247
in order for there to be
consistency.

00:05:15.247 --> 00:05:16.149
[ Laughter ]
I've got aphids.

00:05:16.149 --> 00:05:18.617
I got squirrels.
I got gophers.

00:05:18.617 --> 00:05:21.453
I feel like Elmer Fudd
and Bill Murray in "Caddyshack,"

00:05:21.453 --> 00:05:22.755
trying to kill all these pests.

00:05:22.755 --> 00:05:24.790
I mean, it is --

00:05:24.790 --> 00:05:27.460
The farmer man has a tough life,
let me tell you.

00:05:27.460 --> 00:05:28.794
[ Laughter ]
But it's fun. I love it.

00:05:28.794 --> 00:05:30.429
-Yeah, well, you can tell.

00:05:30.429 --> 00:05:33.132
[ Laughter ]
-No, no. I dig it.

00:05:33.132 --> 00:05:35.635
-Jim, you mentioned
that you have some pests.

00:05:35.635 --> 00:05:37.803
You have some gophers
and the like.

00:05:37.803 --> 00:05:39.371
Do they ever --

00:05:39.371 --> 00:05:42.108
When they eat the plants,

00:05:42.108 --> 00:05:44.277
can you tell the difference
in the rodent?

00:05:44.277 --> 00:05:45.711
[ Laughter ]

00:05:45.711 --> 00:05:47.079
-Yeah, we start hearing

00:05:47.079 --> 00:05:49.014
some Jimi Hendrix
out in the field.

00:05:49.014 --> 00:05:51.216
[ Laughter ]
They're all kind of gathered

00:05:51.216 --> 00:05:54.153
around the fire, you know,
singing along, you know.

00:05:54.153 --> 00:05:56.388
[ Laughter ]
I don't know.

00:05:56.388 --> 00:05:58.324
It doesn't kill them,
that's for sure.

00:05:58.324 --> 00:06:02.428
[ Laughter ]
-Well, that's, I guess, good?

00:06:02.428 --> 00:06:04.530
-Yeah.
-Hey, you also have some time

00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:06.999
for some leisure,
despite being a busy farmer.

00:06:06.999 --> 00:06:10.403
This is a photo you posted,
I think, on Instagram.

00:06:10.403 --> 00:06:12.771 line:0%
This is you diving
into, I guess,

00:06:12.771 --> 00:06:14.373 line:0%
maybe even the river
behind you there.

00:06:14.373 --> 00:06:15.540 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-Yes, it is,

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:17.176 line:0%
right behind me, yeah.

00:06:17.176 --> 00:06:18.444
I was, uh,

00:06:18.444 --> 00:06:19.745
I was running from fire.

00:06:19.745 --> 00:06:21.280
I was being chased by bees.

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:22.915
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:06:22.915 --> 00:06:24.617
-I lost a bet.

00:06:24.617 --> 00:06:25.951
[ Laughter ]
-I got to say, Jim,

00:06:25.951 --> 00:06:28.253
we don't usually have
to pixilate that wide an area,

00:06:28.253 --> 00:06:29.455
so, congratulations.

00:06:29.455 --> 00:06:30.956
[ Laughter ]

00:06:30.956 --> 00:06:31.957
-Well, let me tell you.
-I mean,

00:06:31.957 --> 00:06:34.426
congratulations.
-That water was so cold.

00:06:34.426 --> 00:06:36.662
-That's usually well
out of the safety zone.

00:06:36.662 --> 00:06:37.797
[ Laughter ]

00:06:37.797 --> 00:06:39.131
-The water was so cold,

00:06:39.131 --> 00:06:41.767
parts of my body changed
since then.

00:06:41.767 --> 00:06:43.402
-Well, it's excellent form.

00:06:43.402 --> 00:06:45.705 line:0%
Let me just say,
while we're making jokes here,

00:06:45.705 --> 00:06:47.973 line:0%
that your diving form
is excellent.

00:06:47.973 --> 00:06:49.441 line:0%
[ Laughter ]
-Thank you very much.

00:06:49.441 --> 00:06:52.277
-Hey, I want to talk about some
of your charitable work

00:06:52.277 --> 00:06:53.712
and I know we discussed
this last time,

00:06:53.712 --> 00:06:55.214
but the Last Prisoner project

00:06:55.214 --> 00:06:56.882
is something
you're involved with.

00:06:56.882 --> 00:06:59.018
Actually, especially now,
that we're living in a world

00:06:59.018 --> 00:07:00.519
where we do have, you know,

00:07:00.519 --> 00:07:04.056
legal, you know, marijuana farms
farmers like yourself,

00:07:04.056 --> 00:07:05.991
you're talking about it
as just agriculture now,

00:07:05.991 --> 00:07:07.960
but we have so many people
who are still in prison

00:07:07.960 --> 00:07:09.328
for their marijuana.
-Yeah.

00:07:09.328 --> 00:07:11.964
Well, they were the pioneers
for the cannabis industry.

00:07:11.964 --> 00:07:14.033
They're the ones
that took the arrows.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:18.271
They're the ones that want
to jail for nonviolent

00:07:18.271 --> 00:07:20.706
cannabis crimes,
whether they had,

00:07:20.706 --> 00:07:23.241
you know, an ounce
or three pounds on them,

00:07:23.241 --> 00:07:25.411
they were trying to make
a living for their family.

00:07:25.411 --> 00:07:28.748
And when they get thrown
into prison, it collapses

00:07:28.748 --> 00:07:30.983
that family,
creates more trauma.

00:07:30.983 --> 00:07:33.986
There are 40,000 men
and women incarcerated

00:07:33.986 --> 00:07:36.956
right now for nonviolent
cannabis crimes.

00:07:36.956 --> 00:07:38.390
So the Last Prisoner Project,

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:41.160
it was Steve D'Angelo
and Mary Bailey.

00:07:41.160 --> 00:07:43.162
We are writing letters
to states.

00:07:43.162 --> 00:07:45.197
We've gotten a lot of people
out.

00:07:45.197 --> 00:07:47.499
We got Richard DeLisi
out of Florida.

00:07:47.499 --> 00:07:53.105
He was in jail for 32 years,
the longest cannabis --

00:07:53.105 --> 00:07:57.743
you know, guy incarcerated,
and he's free.

00:07:57.743 --> 00:07:59.579
And so it's happening.
It's happening.

00:07:59.579 --> 00:08:01.280
The state's attorneys
are the people

00:08:01.280 --> 00:08:02.949
that we're really trying to hit

00:08:02.949 --> 00:08:05.918
and it's moving along,
but it never stops.

00:08:05.918 --> 00:08:08.153
So if you want to write
or donate to

00:08:08.153 --> 00:08:10.356
the Last Prisoner Project,

00:08:10.356 --> 00:08:12.291
it'll be a good thing
to do for your community

00:08:12.291 --> 00:08:14.392
and help these families
come back together.

00:08:14.392 --> 00:08:17.529
-Well, congratulations
on your life as a farmer, Jim,

00:08:17.529 --> 00:08:19.832
and congratulations on
the second season of the show.

00:08:19.832 --> 00:08:21.700
It's always a pleasure
to see you.

00:08:21.700 --> 00:08:24.637
-Seth, thank you, and I'll see
you by the beach.

00:08:24.637 --> 00:08:27.639
And by the way, congratulations.

00:08:27.639 --> 00:08:29.908
You know, you can
grow your own, Seth.

00:08:29.908 --> 00:08:31.277
-I can grow my own?

00:08:31.277 --> 00:08:34.714
As fast as I would grow it,
my in-laws would smoke it.

00:08:34.714 --> 00:08:36.315
[ Laughter ]

00:08:36.315 --> 00:08:38.384
Put me out of house and home.
Jim Belushi, everybody.

00:08:38.384 --> 00:08:42.388
"Growing Belushi" airs Wednesday
nights at 10 p.m. on Discovery.

